  "reason": "The current best is config_031 (scvi_n200, resnet50, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted) at 0.6776. The evidence shows scvi_n200 is a strong RNA encoder (0.678 vs 0.639 for pca_n2000 in the same multimodal setting), avgpool outperforms transformer, and weighted fusion beats concat. The one untested dimension on top of config_031 is the image encoder: in the pca_n2000 setting, resnet50 (0.639) and imagenet_vit_l (0.635) were close, but with the stronger scvi_n200 RNA representation the interaction with a higher-capacity image encoder (ViT-L) may shift. config_037 changes only the image encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l, isolating that effect. As the final experiment, this is the highest-probability single-variable extension to potentially exceed 0.678, while avoiding the clearly inferior transformer aggregation or the weaker scgpt encoder."
}

